(i)
"Government" means the State Government;
(j)
"individual care plan" means a comprehensive development plan for a child, based on age and gender specific, needs
and the case history of the child, prepared in consultation with the child, in order to restore the child's self-esteem,
dignity and self-worth and nurture him into a responsible citizen and accordingly, the plan shall address the following,
including but not limited to the needs of a child, namely:-
(i)
health and nutritional needs, including any special needs;
(ii)
emotional and psychological needs;
(iii)
educational and training needs;
(iv)
leisure, creativity and play;
(v)
protection from all kinds of abuse, neglect and maltreatment;
(vi)
life skill training;
